<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Phad painting</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Phad painting is a folk tradition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> in which long cloth scrolls are painted with the stories of local hero-deities such as Pabuji and Devnarayan. The scrolls serve as portable shrines for travelling priest-singers called bhopas, who perform the epics before them at night. The tradition is associated above all with the Joshi family of painters of Shahpura and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhilwara">Bhilwara</a>.</p></div>
